+XS MAINTENANCE
+
+Hash slots returned by hv_fetch must be fetched again after inserting keys
+or calling Perl code that can grow the hash. XPerl can move these slots.
+Keep an owned copy of a value when it must survive a callback or replacement
+of its hash entry. This works with ordinary Perl too and needs no
+XPERL_VERSION conditional.
+
+When reusing a local stack pointer after call_method, refresh it with
+SPAGAIN before pushing arguments for the next call. Let hv_store release
+an existing value when replacing it; an extra decrement frees it twice.
+
+After editing an included XS fragment or C header, force regeneration and
+rebuild before testing:
+
+    touch Chandra.xs
+    make
+    make test
+
+The hash lifetime regression tests run without a display or listener socket:
+
+    make test TEST_FILES=t/69_hash_lifetimes.t
+
+These changes use Perl's public SV, hash and stack APIs. They introduce no
+numeric representation or interpreter-global state assumptions. Threaded,
+debugging, long-double and quadmath builds need their own validation.
+
